{:db/id 17592186087688 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186087435 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "43401830-730c-57d7-8831-9a0580042ffe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Unknown Parameters"}] :question/id #uuid "88c5f90c-9bf9-58a2-a9a2-7c7ff1fc4f8a" :question/math-academy-id "e-14370" :question/problem "The lines $y=2x$ and $kx-2y=-1$ are parallel. What is the value of $k$?" :question/worked-solution "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\n- The line $y=2x$ is in slope-intercept form, and its slope is $2$.\n- To find the slope of the line $kx-2y=-1$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n$kx - 2y|=-1; - 2y|=-kx - 1; 2y|= kx + 1; y|= \\frac{k}{2}x + \\frac{1}{2}$\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $\\dfrac{k}{2}$.\n\nSince the slopes of the two lines must be equal, we must have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{k}{2}=2\n$$\n\nConsequently, $k=4$."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "43401830-730c-57d7-8831-9a0580042ffe" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id 17592186050622}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186088067 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "43401830-730c-57d7-8831-9a0580042ffe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Unknown Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "60eba464-c836-5e56-8019-94413acf4ad6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186085128}] :question/id #uuid "8fe6d174-341f-5856-be44-1861285e1986" :question/math-academy-id "q-214098" :question/problem "The lines $y = 2x + 5$ and $kx + 3y = 9$ are parallel. What is the value of $k$?$k =$\n{{field-1}}"} {:db/id 17592186088068 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "43401830-730c-57d7-8831-9a0580042ffe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Unknown Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "ad8dd299-34e2-51c8-9ba6-9b32de88cb92" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:d